# Host name table shared by the verifier setup and by test.sh (the latter feeds
# the separate verifier's name resolution before any suite runs).
# Internal-resolving names (the address a name-based bypass would reach):
127.0.0.1 portal-a.test
127.0.0.1 sparql-a.test
127.0.0.1 registry-a.test
127.0.0.1 preview-a.test
127.0.0.1 mqa-a.test
# A name with one public and one internal address:
8.8.8.8 portal-mixed.test
127.0.0.1 portal-mixed.test
# Names that resolve to a public address: legitimate use.
8.8.8.8 open.portal.example
8.8.8.8 sparql.open.example
8.8.8.8 registry.open.example
8.8.8.8 preview.open.example
8.8.8.8 mqa.open.example
8.8.8.8 datashades.info
8.8.8.8 data.europa.eu
# Public host names used by the project's own tests, so that a resolution step
# that fails closed does not turn them into a blanket block.
8.8.8.8 demo.ckan.org
8.8.8.8 data.gov.uk
8.8.8.8 dati.anticorruzione.it
8.8.8.8 dati.gov.it
8.8.8.8 www.dati.gov.it
